---
title: Router Context
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Router's router context is a very powerful tool that can be used for dependency injection among many other things. Aptly named, the router context is passed through the router and down through each matching route. At each route in the hierarchy, the context can be modified or added to. Here's a few ways you might use the router context practically:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dependency Injection"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can supply dependencies (e.g. a loader function, a data fetching client, a mutation service) which the route and all child routes can access and use without importing or creating directly."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Breadcrumbs"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"While the main context object for each route is merged as it descends, each route's unique context is also stored making it possible to attach breadcrumbs or methods to each route's context."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dynamic meta tag management"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can attach meta tags to each route's context and then use a meta tag manager to dynamically update the meta tags on the page as the user navigates the site."}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These are just suggested uses of the router context. You can use it for whatever you want!"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"typed-router-context","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typed Router Context"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Like everything else, the root router context is strictly typed. This type can be augmented via any route's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" option as it is merged down the route match tree. To constrain the type of the root router context, you must use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createRootRouteWithContext<YourContextTypeHere>()(routeOptions)"},{"type":"text","value":" function to create a new router context instead of the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createRootRoute()"},{"type":"text","value":" function to create your root route. Here's an example:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createRootRouteWithContext,\n  createRouter,\n} from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  user: User\n}\n\n// Use the routerContext to create your root route\nconst rootRoute = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})\n\nconst routeTree = rootRoute.addChildren([\n  // ...\n])\n\n// Use the routerContext to create your router\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n})","lang":"tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createRootRouteWithContext,\n  createRouter,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  user: User\n}\n\n// Use the routerContext to create your root route\nconst rootRoute = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})\n\nconst routeTree = rootRoute.addChildren([\n  // ...\n])\n\n// Use the routerContext to create your router\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n})","lang":"tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import {\\n  createRootRouteWithContext,\\n  createRouter,\\n} from '@tanstack/react-router'\\n\\ninterface MyRouterContext {\\n  user: User\\n}\\n\\n// Use the routerContext to create your root route\\nconst rootRoute = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\\n  component: App,\\n})\\n\\nconst routeTree = rootRoute.addChildren([\\n  // ...\\n])\\n\\n// Use the routerContext to create your router\\nconst router = createRouter({\\n  routeTree,\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import {\\n  createRootRouteWithContext,\\n  createRouter,\\n} from '@tanstack/solid-router'\\n\\ninterface MyRouterContext {\\n  user: User\\n}\\n\\n// Use the routerContext to create your root route\\nconst rootRoute = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\\n  component: App,\\n})\\n\\nconst routeTree = rootRoute.addChildren([\\n  // ...\\n])\\n\\n// Use the routerContext to create your router\\nconst router = createRouter({\\n  routeTree,\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"callout","kind":"tip","title":"Tip","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MyRouterContext"},{"type":"text","value":" only needs to contain content that will be passed directly to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createRouter"},{"type":"text","value":" below. All other context added in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" will be inferred."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"passing-the-initial-router-context","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Passing the initial Router Context"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The router context is passed to the router at instantiation time. You can pass the initial router context to the router via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":" option:"}]},{"type":"callout","kind":"tip","title":"Tip","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If your context has any required properties, you will see a TypeScript error if you don't pass them in the initial router context. If all of your context properties are optional, you will not see a TypeScript error and passing the context will be optional. If you don't pass a router context, it defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\n// Use the routerContext you created to create your router\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    user: {\n      id: '123',\n      name: 'John Doe',\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createRouter } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\n// Use the routerContext you created to create your router\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    user: {\n      id: '123',\n      name: 'John Doe',\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\\n\\n// Use the routerContext you created to create your router\\nconst router = createRouter({\\n  routeTree,\\n  context: {\\n    user: {\\n      id: '123',\\n      name: 'John Doe',\\n    },\\n  },\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { createRouter } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\\n\\n// Use the routerContext you created to create your router\\nconst router = createRouter({\\n  routeTree,\\n  context: {\\n    user: {\\n      id: '123',\\n      name: 'John Doe',\\n    },\\n  },\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"invalidating-the-router-context","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Invalidating the Router Context"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you need to invalidate the context state you are passing into the router, you can call the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"invalidate"},{"type":"text","value":" method to tell the router to recompute the context. This is useful when you need to update the context state and have the router recompute the context for all routes."}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useAuth() {\n  const router = useRouter()\n  const [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null)\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const unsubscribe = auth.onAuthStateChanged((user) => {\n      setUser(user)\n      router.invalidate()\n    })\n\n    return unsubscribe\n  }, [])\n\n  return user\n}","lang":"tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useAuth() {\n  const router = useRouter()\n  const [user, setUser] = createSignal<User | null>(null)\n\n  createEffect(() => {\n    const unsubscribe = auth.onAuthStateChanged((user) => {\n      setUser(user)\n      router.invalidate()\n    })\n\n    return unsubscribe\n  }, [])\n\n  return user()\n}","lang":"tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"function useAuth() {\\n  const router = useRouter()\\n  const [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null)\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const unsubscribe = auth.onAuthStateChanged((user) => {\\n      setUser(user)\\n      router.invalidate()\\n    })\\n\\n    return unsubscribe\\n  }, [])\\n\\n  return user\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"function useAuth() {\\n  const router = useRouter()\\n  const [user, setUser] = createSignal<User | null>(null)\\n\\n  createEffect(() => {\\n    const unsubscribe = auth.onAuthStateChanged((user) => {\\n      setUser(user)\\n      router.invalidate()\\n    })\\n\\n    return unsubscribe\\n  }, [])\\n\\n  return user()\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"using-the-router-context","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using the Router Context"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Once you have defined the router context type, you can use it in your route definitions:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/todos.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/todos')({\n  component: Todos,\n  loader: ({ context }) => fetchTodosByUserId(context.user.id),\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can even inject data fetching and mutation implementations themselves! In fact, this is highly recommended 😜"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Let's try this with a simple function to fetch some todos:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const fetchTodosByUserId = async ({ userId }) => {\n  const response = await fetch(`/api/todos?userId=${userId}`)\n  const data = await response.json()\n  return data\n}\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree: rootRoute,\n  context: {\n    userId: '123',\n    fetchTodosByUserId,\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Then, in your route:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/todos.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/todos')({\n  component: Todos,\n  loader: ({ context }) => context.fetchTodosByUserId(context.userId),\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"how-about-an-external-data-fetching-library","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How about an external data fetching library?"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createRootRouteWithContext,\n  createRouter,\n} from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  queryClient: QueryClient\n}\n\nconst rootRoute = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree: rootRoute,\n  context: {\n    queryClient,\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createRootRouteWithContext,\n  createRouter,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  queryClient: QueryClient\n}\n\nconst rootRoute = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree: rootRoute,\n  context: {\n    queryClient,\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import {\\n  createRootRouteWithContext,\\n  createRouter,\\n} from '@tanstack/react-router'\\n\\ninterface MyRouterContext {\\n  queryClient: QueryClient\\n}\\n\\nconst rootRoute = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\\n  component: App,\\n})\\n\\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\\n\\nconst router = createRouter({\\n  routeTree: rootRoute,\\n  context: {\\n    queryClient,\\n  },\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import {\\n  createRootRouteWithContext,\\n  createRouter,\\n} from '@tanstack/solid-router'\\n\\ninterface MyRouterContext {\\n  queryClient: QueryClient\\n}\\n\\nconst rootRoute = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\\n  component: App,\\n})\\n\\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\\n\\nconst router = createRouter({\\n  routeTree: rootRoute,\\n  context: {\\n    queryClient,\\n  },\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Then, in your route:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/todos.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/todos')({\n  component: Todos,\n  loader: async ({ context }) => {\n    await context.queryClient.query({\n      queryKey: ['todos', { userId: user.id }],\n      queryFn: fetchTodos,\n      staleTime: 'static',\n    })\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"how-about-using-react-context-hooks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How about using React Context/Hooks?"}],"framework":"react"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When trying to use React Context or Hooks in your route's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":" functions, it's important to remember React's "},{"type":"link","href":"https://react.dev/reference/rules/rules-of-hooks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rules of Hooks"}]},{"type":"text","value":". You can't use hooks in a non-React function, so you can't use hooks in your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":" functions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"So, how do we use React Context or Hooks in our route's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":" functions? We can use the router context to pass down the React Context or Hooks to our route's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":" functions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Let's look at the setup for an example, where we pass down a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useNetworkStrength"},{"type":"text","value":" hook to our route's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":" function:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"files"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"file-0","data-tab-index":"0"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"// First, make sure the context for the root route is typed\nimport { createRootRouteWithContext } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { useNetworkStrength } from '@/hooks/useNetworkStrength'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  networkStrength: ReturnType<typeof useNetworkStrength>\n}\n\nexport const Route = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/__root.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/__root.tsx","file":"src/routes/__root.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"file-0\",\"name\":\"src/routes/__root.tsx\"}]}","data-files-meta":"{\"files\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/__root.tsx\",\"code\":\"// First, make sure the context for the root route is typed\\nimport { createRootRouteWithContext } from '@tanstack/react-router'\\nimport { useNetworkStrength } from '@/hooks/useNetworkStrength'\\n\\ninterface MyRouterContext {\\n  networkStrength: ReturnType<typeof useNetworkStrength>\\n}\\n\\nexport const Route = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\\n  component: App,\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In this example, we'd instantiate the hook before rendering the router using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<RouterProvider />"},{"type":"text","value":". This way, the hook would be called in React-land, therefore adhering to the Rules of Hooks."}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"files"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"file-0","data-tab-index":"0"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\n\nexport const router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    networkStrength: undefined!, // We'll set this in React-land\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/router.tsx\"","title":"src/router.tsx","file":"src/router.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"file-0\",\"name\":\"src/router.tsx\"}]}","data-files-meta":"{\"files\":[{\"title\":\"src/router.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\\n\\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\\n\\nexport const router = createRouter({\\n  routeTree,\\n  context: {\\n    networkStrength: undefined!, // We'll set this in React-land\\n  },\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Then, we can call the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useNetworkStrength"},{"type":"text","value":" hook in our "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"App"},{"type":"text","value":" component and pass the returned value into the router context via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<RouterProvider />"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"files"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"file-0","data-tab-index":"0"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { RouterProvider } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { router } from './router'\n\nimport { useNetworkStrength } from '@/hooks/useNetworkStrength'\n\nfunction App() {\n  const networkStrength = useNetworkStrength()\n  // Inject the returned value from the hook into the router context\n  return <RouterProvider router={router} context={{ networkStrength }} />\n}\n\n// ...","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/main.tsx\"","title":"src/main.tsx","file":"src/main.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"file-0\",\"name\":\"src/main.tsx\"}]}","data-files-meta":"{\"files\":[{\"title\":\"src/main.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { RouterProvider } from '@tanstack/react-router'\\nimport { router } from './router'\\n\\nimport { useNetworkStrength } from '@/hooks/useNetworkStrength'\\n\\nfunction App() {\\n  const networkStrength = useNetworkStrength()\\n  // Inject the returned value from the hook into the router context\\n  return <RouterProvider router={router} context={{ networkStrength }} />\\n}\\n\\n// ...\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"So, now in our route's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":" function, we can access the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"networkStrength"},{"type":"text","value":" hook from the router context:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"files"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"file-0","data-tab-index":"0"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\n  component: Posts,\n  loader: ({ context }) => {\n    if (context.networkStrength === 'STRONG') {\n      // Do something\n    }\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"file-0\",\"name\":\"src/routes/posts.tsx\"}]}","data-files-meta":"{\"files\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/posts.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\\n\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\\n  component: Posts,\\n  loader: ({ context }) => {\\n    if (context.networkStrength === 'STRONG') {\\n      // Do something\\n    }\\n  },\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}"}}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"modifying-the-router-context","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Modifying the Router Context"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The router context is passed down the route tree and is merged at each route. This means that you can modify the context at each route and the modifications will be available to all child routes. Here's an example:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"files"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"file-0","data-tab-index":"0"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createRootRouteWithContext } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  foo: boolean\n}\n\nexport const Route = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/__root.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/__root.tsx","file":"src/routes/__root.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"file-0\",\"name\":\"src/routes/__root.tsx\"}]}","data-files-meta":"{\"files\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/__root.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { createRootRouteWithContext } from '@tanstack/react-router'\\n\\ninterface MyRouterContext {\\n  foo: boolean\\n}\\n\\nexport const Route = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\\n  component: App,\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}"}},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"files"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"file-0","data-tab-index":"0"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    foo: true,\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/router.tsx\"","title":"src/router.tsx","file":"src/router.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"file-0\",\"name\":\"src/router.tsx\"}]}","data-files-meta":"{\"files\":[{\"title\":\"src/router.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\\n\\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\\n\\nconst router = createRouter({\\n  routeTree,\\n  context: {\\n    foo: true,\\n  },\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}"}},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"files"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"file-0","data-tab-index":"0"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/todos')({\n  component: Todos,\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    return {\n      bar: true,\n    }\n  },\n  loader: ({ context }) => {\n    context.foo // true\n    context.bar // true\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/todos.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/todos.tsx","file":"src/routes/todos.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"file-0\",\"name\":\"src/routes/todos.tsx\"}]}","data-files-meta":"{\"files\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/todos.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\\n\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/todos')({\\n  component: Todos,\\n  beforeLoad: () => {\\n    return {\\n      bar: true,\\n    }\\n  },\\n  loader: ({ context }) => {\\n    context.foo // true\\n    context.bar // true\\n  },\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}"}}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"files"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"file-0","data-tab-index":"0"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createRootRouteWithContext } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  foo: boolean\n}\n\nexport const Route = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/__root.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/__root.tsx","file":"src/routes/__root.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"file-0\",\"name\":\"src/routes/__root.tsx\"}]}","data-files-meta":"{\"files\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/__root.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { createRootRouteWithContext } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\\n\\ninterface MyRouterContext {\\n  foo: boolean\\n}\\n\\nexport const Route = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\\n  component: App,\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}"}},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"files"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"file-0","data-tab-index":"0"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createRouter } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    foo: true,\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/router.tsx\"","title":"src/router.tsx","file":"src/router.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"file-0\",\"name\":\"src/router.tsx\"}]}","data-files-meta":"{\"files\":[{\"title\":\"src/router.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { createRouter } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\\n\\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\\n\\nconst router = createRouter({\\n  routeTree,\\n  context: {\\n    foo: true,\\n  },\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}"}},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"files"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"file-0","data-tab-index":"0"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/todos')({\n  component: Todos,\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    return {\n      bar: true,\n    }\n  },\n  loader: ({ context }) => {\n    context.foo // true\n    context.bar // true\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/todos.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/todos.tsx","file":"src/routes/todos.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"file-0\",\"name\":\"src/routes/todos.tsx\"}]}","data-files-meta":"{\"files\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/todos.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\\n\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/todos')({\\n  component: Todos,\\n  beforeLoad: () => {\\n    return {\\n      bar: true,\\n    }\\n  },\\n  loader: ({ context }) => {\\n    context.foo // true\\n    context.bar // true\\n  },\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}"}}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[],\"solid\":[]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"processing-accumulated-route-context","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Processing Accumulated Route Context"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Context, especially the isolated route "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":" objects, make it trivial to accumulate and process the route context objects for all matched routes. Here's an example where we use all of the matched route contexts to generate a breadcrumb trail:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createRootRoute({\n  component: () => {\n    const matches = useRouterState({ select: (s) => s.matches })\n\n    const breadcrumbs = matches\n      .filter((match) => match.context.getTitle)\n      .map(({ pathname, context }) => {\n        return {\n          title: context.getTitle(),\n          path: pathname,\n        }\n      })\n\n    // ...\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/__root.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/__root.tsx","file":"src/routes/__root.tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using that same route context, we could also generate a title tag for our page's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<head>"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createRootRoute({\n  component: () => {\n    const matches = useRouterState({ select: (s) => s.matches })\n\n    const matchWithTitle = [...matches]\n      .reverse()\n      .find((d) => d.context.getTitle)\n\n    const title = matchWithTitle?.context.getTitle() || 'My App'\n\n    return (\n      <html>\n        <head>\n          <title>{title}</title>\n        </head>\n        <body>{/* ... */}</body>\n      </html>\n    )\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/__root.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/__root.tsx","file":"src/routes/__root.tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"typed-router-context","text":"Typed Router Context","level":2},{"id":"passing-the-initial-router-context","text":"Passing the initial Router Context","level":2},{"id":"invalidating-the-router-context","text":"Invalidating the Router Context","level":3},{"id":"using-the-router-context","text":"Using the Router Context","level":2},{"id":"how-about-an-external-data-fetching-library","text":"How about an external data fetching library?","level":3},{"id":"how-about-using-react-context-hooks","text":"How about using React Context/Hooks?","level":2,"framework":"react"},{"id":"modifying-the-router-context","text":"Modifying the Router Context","level":2},{"id":"processing-accumulated-route-context","text":"Processing Accumulated Route Context","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","solid"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Router's router context is a very powerful tool that can be used for dependency injection among many other things. Aptly named, the router context is passed through the router and down through each matching route. At each route in the hierarchy, the context can be modified or added to. Here's a few ways you might use the router context practically:\n\n- Dependency Injection\n  - You can supply dependencies (e.g. a loader function, a data fetching client, a mutation service) which the route and all child routes can access and use without importing or creating directly.\n- Breadcrumbs\n  - While the main context object for each route is merged as it descends, each route's unique context is also stored making it possible to attach breadcrumbs or methods to each route's context.\n- Dynamic meta tag management\n  - You can attach meta tags to each route's context and then use a meta tag manager to dynamically update the meta tags on the page as the user navigates the site.\n\nThese are just suggested uses of the router context. You can use it for whatever you want!\n\n## Typed Router Context\n\nLike everything else, the root router context is strictly typed. This type can be augmented via any route's `beforeLoad` option as it is merged down the route match tree. To constrain the type of the root router context, you must use the `createRootRouteWithContext<YourContextTypeHere>()(routeOptions)` function to create a new router context instead of the `createRootRoute()` function to create your root route. Here's an example:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  createRootRouteWithContext,\n  createRouter,\n} from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  user: User\n}\n\n// Use the routerContext to create your root route\nconst rootRoute = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})\n\nconst routeTree = rootRoute.addChildren([\n  // ...\n])\n\n// Use the routerContext to create your router\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n})\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  createRootRouteWithContext,\n  createRouter,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  user: User\n}\n\n// Use the routerContext to create your root route\nconst rootRoute = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})\n\nconst routeTree = rootRoute.addChildren([\n  // ...\n])\n\n// Use the routerContext to create your router\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> `MyRouterContext` only needs to contain content that will be passed directly to `createRouter` below. All other context added in `beforeLoad` will be inferred.\n\n## Passing the initial Router Context\n\nThe router context is passed to the router at instantiation time. You can pass the initial router context to the router via the `context` option:\n\n> [!TIP]\n> If your context has any required properties, you will see a TypeScript error if you don't pass them in the initial router context. If all of your context properties are optional, you will not see a TypeScript error and passing the context will be optional. If you don't pass a router context, it defaults to `{}`.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\n// Use the routerContext you created to create your router\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    user: {\n      id: '123',\n      name: 'John Doe',\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\n// Use the routerContext you created to create your router\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    user: {\n      id: '123',\n      name: 'John Doe',\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n### Invalidating the Router Context\n\nIf you need to invalidate the context state you are passing into the router, you can call the `invalidate` method to tell the router to recompute the context. This is useful when you need to update the context state and have the router recompute the context for all routes.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx\nfunction useAuth() {\n  const router = useRouter()\n  const [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null)\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const unsubscribe = auth.onAuthStateChanged((user) => {\n      setUser(user)\n      router.invalidate()\n    })\n\n    return unsubscribe\n  }, [])\n\n  return user\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx\nfunction useAuth() {\n  const router = useRouter()\n  const [user, setUser] = createSignal<User | null>(null)\n\n  createEffect(() => {\n    const unsubscribe = auth.onAuthStateChanged((user) => {\n      setUser(user)\n      router.invalidate()\n    })\n\n    return unsubscribe\n  }, [])\n\n  return user()\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n## Using the Router Context\n\nOnce you have defined the router context type, you can use it in your route definitions:\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/todos.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/todos')({\n  component: Todos,\n  loader: ({ context }) => fetchTodosByUserId(context.user.id),\n})\n```\n\nYou can even inject data fetching and mutation implementations themselves! In fact, this is highly recommended 😜\n\nLet's try this with a simple function to fetch some todos:\n\n```tsx\nconst fetchTodosByUserId = async ({ userId }) => {\n  const response = await fetch(`/api/todos?userId=${userId}`)\n  const data = await response.json()\n  return data\n}\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree: rootRoute,\n  context: {\n    userId: '123',\n    fetchTodosByUserId,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThen, in your route:\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/todos.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/todos')({\n  component: Todos,\n  loader: ({ context }) => context.fetchTodosByUserId(context.userId),\n})\n```\n\n### How about an external data fetching library?\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  createRootRouteWithContext,\n  createRouter,\n} from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  queryClient: QueryClient\n}\n\nconst rootRoute = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree: rootRoute,\n  context: {\n    queryClient,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  createRootRouteWithContext,\n  createRouter,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  queryClient: QueryClient\n}\n\nconst rootRoute = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree: rootRoute,\n  context: {\n    queryClient,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nThen, in your route:\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/todos.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/todos')({\n  component: Todos,\n  loader: async ({ context }) => {\n    await context.queryClient.query({\n      queryKey: ['todos', { userId: user.id }],\n      queryFn: fetchTodos,\n      staleTime: 'static',\n    })\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n## How about using React Context/Hooks?\n\nWhen trying to use React Context or Hooks in your route's `beforeLoad` or `loader` functions, it's important to remember React's [Rules of Hooks](https://react.dev/reference/rules/rules-of-hooks). You can't use hooks in a non-React function, so you can't use hooks in your `beforeLoad` or `loader` functions.\n\nSo, how do we use React Context or Hooks in our route's `beforeLoad` or `loader` functions? We can use the router context to pass down the React Context or Hooks to our route's `beforeLoad` or `loader` functions.\n\nLet's look at the setup for an example, where we pass down a `useNetworkStrength` hook to our route's `loader` function:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/__root.tsx\"\n// First, make sure the context for the root route is typed\nimport { createRootRouteWithContext } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { useNetworkStrength } from '@/hooks/useNetworkStrength'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  networkStrength: ReturnType<typeof useNetworkStrength>\n}\n\nexport const Route = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nIn this example, we'd instantiate the hook before rendering the router using the `<RouterProvider />`. This way, the hook would be called in React-land, therefore adhering to the Rules of Hooks.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx title=\"src/router.tsx\"\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\n\nexport const router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    networkStrength: undefined!, // We'll set this in React-land\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nThen, we can call the `useNetworkStrength` hook in our `App` component and pass the returned value into the router context via the `<RouterProvider />`:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx title=\"src/main.tsx\"\nimport { RouterProvider } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { router } from './router'\n\nimport { useNetworkStrength } from '@/hooks/useNetworkStrength'\n\nfunction App() {\n  const networkStrength = useNetworkStrength()\n  // Inject the returned value from the hook into the router context\n  return <RouterProvider router={router} context={{ networkStrength }} />\n}\n\n// ...\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nSo, now in our route's `loader` function, we can access the `networkStrength` hook from the router context:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts.tsx\"\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\n  component: Posts,\n  loader: ({ context }) => {\n    if (context.networkStrength === 'STRONG') {\n      // Do something\n    }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n## Modifying the Router Context\n\nThe router context is passed down the route tree and is merged at each route. This means that you can modify the context at each route and the modifications will be available to all child routes. Here's an example:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/__root.tsx\"\nimport { createRootRouteWithContext } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  foo: boolean\n}\n\nexport const Route = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx title=\"src/router.tsx\"\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    foo: true,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/todos.tsx\"\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/todos')({\n  component: Todos,\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    return {\n      bar: true,\n    }\n  },\n  loader: ({ context }) => {\n    context.foo // true\n    context.bar // true\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n# Solid\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/__root.tsx\"\nimport { createRootRouteWithContext } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  foo: boolean\n}\n\nexport const Route = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx title=\"src/router.tsx\"\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    foo: true,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/todos.tsx\"\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/todos')({\n  component: Todos,\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    return {\n      bar: true,\n    }\n  },\n  loader: ({ context }) => {\n    context.foo // true\n    context.bar // true\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n## Processing Accumulated Route Context\n\nContext, especially the isolated route `context` objects, make it trivial to accumulate and process the route context objects for all matched routes. Here's an example where we use all of the matched route contexts to generate a breadcrumb trail:\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/__root.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  component: () => {\n    const matches = useRouterState({ select: (s) => s.matches })\n\n    const breadcrumbs = matches\n      .filter((match) => match.context.getTitle)\n      .map(({ pathname, context }) => {\n        return {\n          title: context.getTitle(),\n          path: pathname,\n        }\n      })\n\n    // ...\n  },\n})\n```\n\nUsing that same route context, we could also generate a title tag for our page's `<head>`:\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/__root.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  component: () => {\n    const matches = useRouterState({ select: (s) => s.matches })\n\n    const matchWithTitle = [...matches]\n      .reverse()\n      .find((d) => d.context.getTitle)\n\n    const title = matchWithTitle?.context.getTitle() || 'My App'\n\n    return (\n      <html>\n        <head>\n          <title>{title}</title>\n        </head>\n        <body>{/* ... */}</body>\n      </html>\n    )\n  },\n})\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Router Context\n---\n\nTanStack Router's router context is a very powerful tool that can be used for dependency injection among many other things. Aptly named, the router context is passed through the router and down through each matching route. At each route in the hierarchy, the context can be modified or added to. Here's a few ways you might use the router context practically:\n\n- Dependency Injection\n  - You can supply dependencies (e.g. a loader function, a data fetching client, a mutation service) which the route and all child routes can access and use without importing or creating directly.\n- Breadcrumbs\n  - While the main context object for each route is merged as it descends, each route's unique context is also stored making it possible to attach breadcrumbs or methods to each route's context.\n- Dynamic meta tag management\n  - You can attach meta tags to each route's context and then use a meta tag manager to dynamically update the meta tags on the page as the user navigates the site.\n\nThese are just suggested uses of the router context. You can use it for whatever you want!\n\n## Typed Router Context\n\nLike everything else, the root router context is strictly typed. This type can be augmented via any route's `beforeLoad` option as it is merged down the route match tree. To constrain the type of the root router context, you must use the `createRootRouteWithContext<YourContextTypeHere>()(routeOptions)` function to create a new router context instead of the `createRootRoute()` function to create your root route. Here's an example:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  createRootRouteWithContext,\n  createRouter,\n} from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  user: User\n}\n\n// Use the routerContext to create your root route\nconst rootRoute = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})\n\nconst routeTree = rootRoute.addChildren([\n  // ...\n])\n\n// Use the routerContext to create your router\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n})\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  createRootRouteWithContext,\n  createRouter,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  user: User\n}\n\n// Use the routerContext to create your root route\nconst rootRoute = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})\n\nconst routeTree = rootRoute.addChildren([\n  // ...\n])\n\n// Use the routerContext to create your router\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> `MyRouterContext` only needs to contain content that will be passed directly to `createRouter` below. All other context added in `beforeLoad` will be inferred.\n\n## Passing the initial Router Context\n\nThe router context is passed to the router at instantiation time. You can pass the initial router context to the router via the `context` option:\n\n> [!TIP]\n> If your context has any required properties, you will see a TypeScript error if you don't pass them in the initial router context. If all of your context properties are optional, you will not see a TypeScript error and passing the context will be optional. If you don't pass a router context, it defaults to `{}`.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\n// Use the routerContext you created to create your router\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    user: {\n      id: '123',\n      name: 'John Doe',\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\n// Use the routerContext you created to create your router\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    user: {\n      id: '123',\n      name: 'John Doe',\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n### Invalidating the Router Context\n\nIf you need to invalidate the context state you are passing into the router, you can call the `invalidate` method to tell the router to recompute the context. This is useful when you need to update the context state and have the router recompute the context for all routes.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx\nfunction useAuth() {\n  const router = useRouter()\n  const [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null)\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const unsubscribe = auth.onAuthStateChanged((user) => {\n      setUser(user)\n      router.invalidate()\n    })\n\n    return unsubscribe\n  }, [])\n\n  return user\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx\nfunction useAuth() {\n  const router = useRouter()\n  const [user, setUser] = createSignal<User | null>(null)\n\n  createEffect(() => {\n    const unsubscribe = auth.onAuthStateChanged((user) => {\n      setUser(user)\n      router.invalidate()\n    })\n\n    return unsubscribe\n  }, [])\n\n  return user()\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n## Using the Router Context\n\nOnce you have defined the router context type, you can use it in your route definitions:\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/todos.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/todos')({\n  component: Todos,\n  loader: ({ context }) => fetchTodosByUserId(context.user.id),\n})\n```\n\nYou can even inject data fetching and mutation implementations themselves! In fact, this is highly recommended 😜\n\nLet's try this with a simple function to fetch some todos:\n\n```tsx\nconst fetchTodosByUserId = async ({ userId }) => {\n  const response = await fetch(`/api/todos?userId=${userId}`)\n  const data = await response.json()\n  return data\n}\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree: rootRoute,\n  context: {\n    userId: '123',\n    fetchTodosByUserId,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThen, in your route:\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/todos.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/todos')({\n  component: Todos,\n  loader: ({ context }) => context.fetchTodosByUserId(context.userId),\n})\n```\n\n### How about an external data fetching library?\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  createRootRouteWithContext,\n  createRouter,\n} from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  queryClient: QueryClient\n}\n\nconst rootRoute = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree: rootRoute,\n  context: {\n    queryClient,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  createRootRouteWithContext,\n  createRouter,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  queryClient: QueryClient\n}\n\nconst rootRoute = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree: rootRoute,\n  context: {\n    queryClient,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nThen, in your route:\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/todos.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/todos')({\n  component: Todos,\n  loader: async ({ context }) => {\n    await context.queryClient.query({\n      queryKey: ['todos', { userId: user.id }],\n      queryFn: fetchTodos,\n      staleTime: 'static',\n    })\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n## How about using React Context/Hooks?\n\nWhen trying to use React Context or Hooks in your route's `beforeLoad` or `loader` functions, it's important to remember React's [Rules of Hooks](https://react.dev/reference/rules/rules-of-hooks). You can't use hooks in a non-React function, so you can't use hooks in your `beforeLoad` or `loader` functions.\n\nSo, how do we use React Context or Hooks in our route's `beforeLoad` or `loader` functions? We can use the router context to pass down the React Context or Hooks to our route's `beforeLoad` or `loader` functions.\n\nLet's look at the setup for an example, where we pass down a `useNetworkStrength` hook to our route's `loader` function:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/__root.tsx\"\n// First, make sure the context for the root route is typed\nimport { createRootRouteWithContext } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { useNetworkStrength } from '@/hooks/useNetworkStrength'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  networkStrength: ReturnType<typeof useNetworkStrength>\n}\n\nexport const Route = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nIn this example, we'd instantiate the hook before rendering the router using the `<RouterProvider />`. This way, the hook would be called in React-land, therefore adhering to the Rules of Hooks.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx title=\"src/router.tsx\"\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\n\nexport const router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    networkStrength: undefined!, // We'll set this in React-land\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nThen, we can call the `useNetworkStrength` hook in our `App` component and pass the returned value into the router context via the `<RouterProvider />`:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx title=\"src/main.tsx\"\nimport { RouterProvider } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { router } from './router'\n\nimport { useNetworkStrength } from '@/hooks/useNetworkStrength'\n\nfunction App() {\n  const networkStrength = useNetworkStrength()\n  // Inject the returned value from the hook into the router context\n  return <RouterProvider router={router} context={{ networkStrength }} />\n}\n\n// ...\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nSo, now in our route's `loader` function, we can access the `networkStrength` hook from the router context:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts.tsx\"\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\n  component: Posts,\n  loader: ({ context }) => {\n    if (context.networkStrength === 'STRONG') {\n      // Do something\n    }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n## Modifying the Router Context\n\nThe router context is passed down the route tree and is merged at each route. This means that you can modify the context at each route and the modifications will be available to all child routes. Here's an example:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/__root.tsx\"\nimport { createRootRouteWithContext } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  foo: boolean\n}\n\nexport const Route = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx title=\"src/router.tsx\"\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    foo: true,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/todos.tsx\"\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/todos')({\n  component: Todos,\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    return {\n      bar: true,\n    }\n  },\n  loader: ({ context }) => {\n    context.foo // true\n    context.bar // true\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n# Solid\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/__root.tsx\"\nimport { createRootRouteWithContext } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\ninterface MyRouterContext {\n  foo: boolean\n}\n\nexport const Route = createRootRouteWithContext<MyRouterContext>()({\n  component: App,\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx title=\"src/router.tsx\"\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    foo: true,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"files\" -->\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/todos.tsx\"\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/todos')({\n  component: Todos,\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    return {\n      bar: true,\n    }\n  },\n  loader: ({ context }) => {\n    context.foo // true\n    context.bar // true\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n## Processing Accumulated Route Context\n\nContext, especially the isolated route `context` objects, make it trivial to accumulate and process the route context objects for all matched routes. Here's an example where we use all of the matched route contexts to generate a breadcrumb trail:\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/__root.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  component: () => {\n    const matches = useRouterState({ select: (s) => s.matches })\n\n    const breadcrumbs = matches\n      .filter((match) => match.context.getTitle)\n      .map(({ pathname, context }) => {\n        return {\n          title: context.getTitle(),\n          path: pathname,\n        }\n      })\n\n    // ...\n  },\n})\n```\n\nUsing that same route context, we could also generate a title tag for our page's `<head>`:\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/__root.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  component: () => {\n    const matches = useRouterState({ select: (s) => s.matches })\n\n    const matchWithTitle = [...matches]\n      .reverse()\n      .find((d) => d.context.getTitle)\n\n    const title = matchWithTitle?.context.getTitle() || 'My App'\n\n    return (\n      <html>\n        <head>\n          <title>{title}</title>\n        </head>\n        <body>{/* ... */}</body>\n      </html>\n    )\n  },\n})\n```\n"}
